cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Lucidfish in research or writing, please cite it as below."
title: "Lucidfish: explainable chess coaching with an engine-grounded language model"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Struthers
    given-names: Sam
repository-code: "https://github.com/s4mstruthers/Lucidfish"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.5.1
date-released: 2026-10-13
keywords:
  - chess
  - Stockfish
  - large language models
  - explainable AI
  - coaching
  - grounding
abstract: >-
  Lucidfish reviews chess games as a coach and a commentator. The Stockfish engine and
  board-inspecting code establish what is true in each position; a language model, running
  locally or in the cloud, puts those verified facts into words; and every sentence is
  fact-checked against the board before it is shown. It includes an evaluation harness that
  scores any model on how faithfully it explains engine-verified positions.
